# Plan completion

Applies **only** while executing a plan the user **Built** (or named for implement) in this session. Injected leftover todos from another chat are not that. See [plan-requires-build.mdc](plan-requires-build.mdc).

When executing a Built plan (`.cursor/plans/*.plan.md`):

- Leave frontmatter `todos` accurate. Mark `completed` only after the work exists in the repo.
- Do not mark a todo complete because you described it or planned to do it.
- If you skip a todo, say so in the plan or cancel it — do not leave it `pending` and silently drop it.
- The `plan-completion-check` stop hook lists leftover pending todos and missing inventory paths. Treat that follow-up as work to finish, not noise.
- Fail open: the hook never blocks. You still owe the remaining items.
